   265	*Two hundred and seventy-seventh day. The read: the ground, at the landing, from the post's foot to the old sill. In earnest. Deployment since the Line: thirty.*
   266	
   267	"You asked him to our board," said Lira.
   268	
   269	"I told him where it was."
   270	
   271	"That's asking."
   272	
   273	"Then I asked."
   274	
   275	She was a long while answering. When she did, it was in a small cross voice that he had not heard out of her since a rail on a bluff.
   276	
   277	"I don't know what face to bring," she said.

