+4. First six: `Pike made the new cloth that`
+   Last six: `pack, bent to his knots again.`
+   Listening notes: Clean. Pike frames and repeats each cloth line; Teague's four retain their fixed roles, and the tall spear-carrier is explicitly a man. `the boy` is Teague's young member.
+5. First six: `The reeds came down the river`
+   Last six: `and began on its other cheek.`
+   Listening notes: Clean. Lira/Cael alternate through the hurdle work without attribution drift; the ferryman's short interjections remain separate. Shadow stays refused and no deployment number changes.
