### Lane A second-ear join — chapter 14

- Sentence before: `"I do not say it as a complaint. I am trying to enter it correctly. I have not gone into a room in forty years that did not turn to see who had come. I have just stood within fifty yards of a thing that hunts, and it went over me as it went over a bush. I find that I have no column for that."`
- Edited join sentence: `He was a little out of breath, and he had kept his place, a dozen strides back, so that he had to pitch the words forward.`
- Sentence after: `"You were a post. A post is what it doesn't look at."`
