140:- **The book's last line and the six restored units** (Gault's last note; the personnel query; the waystation board; "You couldn't read me…"; Cael's reply to Daeva; the closing exchange) are verbatim from the protected wording, with only the edition's mandatory changes ("Since my Kindling"; "Nine fragments"; the personnel query's teaching-assistant role, calendar and house frame).
146:## 48. Book 7 reconciliation to edition Book 6 (coordinator defaults, 2026-10-11)
148:- **Season-blind and feet/yards, continued into Book 7** (as #37 O1 and #42 did for Books 5 and 6). Named seasons and metric units are replaced, minimally, INCLUDING inside Book 7's protected lines (for example "Spring. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes." becomes "After the thaw. …"; "Twelve hundred and fifty-six meters, and a piece." becomes the same distance in yards). Generic "season" and "month" stay. Every changed protected line is listed, old and new, in `book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-APPLIED.md`; the owner may restore any or all when the series calendar is ruled.
150:- **The birthday:** day 102 past the Line stands, never beside a season, a month order or a count back to the last birthday. By the edition's own day counts the two birthdays fall roughly 225 days apart (Book 6's mid-year, the year's close near day 207, then 102 days). The prose never states it; the series calendar remains the owner's to rule (#35, #42).
177:- **#56 (Book 8 Movement 2 or 3, Thornwater).** `"Five months and twenty days."` — Lira's arm, from the Ring to its release. It is true on the plan's day count (day 96 to day 265–266) but only if a month is thirty days, and #35 says the prose never states month lengths. **Default:** verbatim. Options: keep; "A hundred and seventy days."; or a wording without a figure.
180:Applied under standing decisions, and listed old and new in `B7-RECONCILIATION-APPLIED.md` so any can be restored: Book 8's named seasons (#48) and its three "five years" counts since Kindling (#18), the same changes Books 5–7 made.
191:The protected unit (BOOK_MAP §10 Tier A 5) reads "Deep layer. Sequence initiated" [a Compact date] "Unreadable. Not halted. Running. Correlated with classification event —". The source prints no value either ("She gave the date. It was a Compact date, a registry year and a day in it"). Sol's plan audit asked for an owner-supplied date. **Coordinator default:** the edition does as the source does — the sheet shows a date in the office's reckoning and the page never gives its figures, in Movement 2 or at the spring in Movement 3 (where Cael knows it for his Kindling day; no span of years is computed, #18). If the owner wants a printed registry date, it has to be minted and reconciled with #35/#42 (the series calendar), and ch12 and the spring scene re-touched.

