editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/LANE-A-REPORT.md:90:Examined and kept (20): ch1:145 "It billed him now" (a trial's cost, in his own log diction); ch2:167 "as level as a count" (her count of five follows); ch3:197 "Teague priced it" (a real cost is weighed); ch5:217 the bill sent to the smith (a copper); ch6:175 "as she would have entered it" (Karis's own word); ch6:231 and ch15:181 "as he counted any room" (a count tableau; a tactical count of eight); ch7:245 the chin "by the width of a finger" (Teague's sign, now two of four); ch11:81 "last year's price, to the copper" (the price is what he is ruling on); ch16:197 "enter the breaking as a fault" (he is writing the log); ch19:119 "She priced them" (Oryn's word, in her mouth and Lira's); ch20:35 "since he counted anything" (the one use of that formula left standing); ch21:165 "paid tonight in a coin" (a debt is tracked); ch22:55, ch23:79, ch25:153 and 251, ch26:245 "told it no" at the sill, the gates and the iron door (a fragment refused each time); ch27:67 "He counted his strides instead" (the figures follow); ch27:131 "the width of a finger" (Karis's measured gaps); ch28:145 "longer than he liked to count"; ch29:61 "Cael had priced that man a great many ways" (what Brom is worth is the scene); ch30:163 "as he counted anything. It was six words." (beside a protected log line); ch30:209 "the width of a hair" (the lamp's movement is the measure at issue). The courier's flat, the four hand-signs, every log and tally, all money and every healer's count were left alone.
