editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:372:23. **Pike (S2; S17):** "What'd he do?" / "Nothing," Vastin said. "Out here. Nothing yet." / "Then he's nothing yet." And the 297th line: *Treswick. Survey read. Bearing.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:395:- **S5:** "You keep drafting orders." / "Habit." / "Out here the habit's the tell." … "Draft nothing. Just look." / "Two copies of one ignorance." Close: "Six years," Karis said. "They measured all of it. They graded it — the sites are ranked by something, and it's the same something in the kit, and I can't read either one." … "Everything I can't read points at the same place." / "Treswick," / "The archive under it. Cleon." / "Who's Cleon?" / "The only historical-Path practitioner registered west of the Line. If the language is anywhere, it's under his hands. A day and a half." … "And then I find out whether I've been right for five years or wrong for five years, and I don't know which I'm more afraid of." [OWNER-pending #52]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:396:- **S6:** "I'm not an archive person." / "Leaving and routing are different verbs. I'm doing the second." / "You go inside, you don't go near the station. Not the steps, not the square. You promise me in that log of yours, because I've seen what the log does to you." / the log entry: "The fork. Oryn north; five holds; routing, not the other verb. Her term, given at the fire, taken in the log because that's the form she'll take it in: inside Treswick I do not go near the station. Not the steps. Not the square. Written here so she can read it, and so I can." / "Bring me whatever walks out of that archive with you. All of it." / "Not the steps," … "Not the square."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:397:- **S7 log:** "Ran the reading on myself again. Same nothing at the center. I think the reading can't do it — you can't measure a stillness with a thing that only feels movement. I need an instrument for what doesn't move. Karis says there's a man in Treswick who reads how things are built. Maybe that's the instrument. Maybe I'm about to hand a stranger the one question I've never let anyone hold. Tomorrow. The walls are close enough now to have a color." ("color" stands in the log, per ruling 19.) Also: "You were the instrument," … "I was the error." / "I declined to read you a second time. You know that. What you do not know is why."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:444:- **C7 — Reveal locus.** CANON_RULES says "ancient records in edge-territory ruins"; the bible says a "pre-Compact archive at a border city". The source stages both: the leaf is in the Treswick archive and its key is the ruins' carvings. **Flag for the bible pass.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:447:- **C10 — The "first entry inside walls".** S14 calls the 292nd inventory "the first entry in the plain hand that had ever been made in a city", but daily log entries are written inside Treswick on the 282nd, 285th and 290th. **Edition:** it is the first *inventory* (the year's ledger form) written inside walls.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:458:New cold-term, Treswick and leg episodes [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] must leave each of these intact:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:472:- **Cleon's name** is first heard by Cael on the 280th. **Treswick and the Deepstacks** are first spoken aloud at the 268th table.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:475:- **Cael reads pages the wrong way round** until somewhere on Treswick's stair, and no longer does by the 297th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:484:**Existing names stay exactly as canon has them.** Never "Halcenvane" on the page; use "the academy above Ostrand". The registry collisions are untouched (OWNER-DECISIONS #6). **Audiobook read-through list** (carried): Cleon/Cael (KLEE-on/KAYL; never in one spoken run); Span/Stair; Treswick/Ternhall (keep them out of one spoken inventory); the O-onset stack Oryn/Oxhollow/Ostrand; Pike/Fiske. Places minted by canon only: Treswick, the Deepstacks, the Sunken Span, "the court" (description), the shoulder hold, the cut, the pass. **Do not name new holds** on Oryn's route. Use Oxhollow or Thornwater, or none.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:490:Book 9 opens with: the court's centre (no edge; "the same kind of made"); the Rune finding that nobody else knows; the dark Arbiter; the instruments trending wrong; the crack; Vastin unadmitted (Book 9 stages his formal request and the 3–2 vote, with Seln deciding); Oryn's three future holds and "After the thaw: bring the map, and lie still when I say."; Teague's "After the next thaw" and his grief; Cleon under Treswick; thirteen fragments; the leaf's copies with the gap drawn; the mule with Oryn; Cael remains nineteen at the Book 9 opening. Do not place or calculate his next birthday until the owner rules the series calendar. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] Book 9 owns the tomb in the deepest edge territory, the word "recurrence", the Compact's open fracture (Seln's documents), and the Quieting's first visible spread into a city's outer districts. **Do not pre-pay any of these in Book 8.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:48:**He does not know:** that the index is a grade; the Architect; Treswick's archive or Cleon; anything Vastin carries; that instruments will read wrong in his hands. The last is discovered on the 168th (Book 7 ends with the instruments reading TRUE in his hand; Book 8 Ch1 owns the first hair). [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: coordinator ruling] (restored: entry content the amendment's replacement had dropped)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:97:| Hesk, Vell | Letters. Hesk's next parcel (the dividers) arrives in Treswick on the 292nd. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:128:- **"West" was first said aloud at the six-person table on the 268th**, in Karis's protected speech (Treswick, the last Compact city on the Line; the registry office on the old town; the Deepstacks under it). Cleon is not named. The protected closing log is on the 270th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:151:- **Her case, as said on the 268th (flag; the place itself is now given only in her restored protected speech):** mine are the two steps before it: "I think that they are instructions." (the same forty-one kinds in the same order on three floors; a line that carries the circle's own measure), and that a key to the index exists and "is kept". The hide lies on Seln's oilcloth with the brass along its pencil line. Then the coordinator's three joins and the protected speech, in which **"west", "Treswick" and "the Deepstacks" are said aloud for the first time**. My earlier description of the archive, of the provision and of Karis's certificate is gone. **After the speech, mine:** Seln adds only what the speech does not have (a gate with a book in it; a station on its crown; the paper that executes "on the hour when any of us shows a certificate inside the Line"; one file not shut); Lira's certificate ("Iron, Rank One, with a seal on it"); Cael's "A registry's where they file you"; no ruling. The scene closes on "her first two words", which none of the six had ever said aloud as a place to go.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:170:**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three. **She has made her case to six** (the 268th): instructions; an index with a key that is kept; and then, in her protected speech, west, Treswick, the registry office on the old town, the Deepstacks under it, the old scholars' provision for a registered historical-studies practitioner, which she is not, and "a man there who is" (unnamed). She said the sentence whole to Cael on the 263rd, without the word west. She cannot read the four signs and has put no meaning on the stroke and the bar. She knows how the kit's cord is used and has taught the five. She has entered the anomaly as *Cause: not found. No inference entered.* and has written no sentence joining it to anything. Fifty-two sheets; the hide; the kit; the dead man's ledger, open now; a hair in her notebook. She keeps the purse.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:186:**Words said aloud for the first time.** *West* (as the place to go), *Treswick* and *the Deepstacks*: all three by Karis, in her protected speech at the board on the 268th, and by nobody before it. Cael writes *West, and inside* on the 270th. Not said at all: Cleon's name; Vastin's.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:199:- **Seln:** his locked case remains shut; he taught nobody; he has begun a second hazel wand and reaches forty notches on day 270; he already recognized Treswick/Deepstacks when Karis said them (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:247,253,283`). He still does not explain the rival clock.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:215:- **The three papers.** (1) **The records:** a seat-courier's flat of waxed leather; six taped rows, a year to a row, of survey abstracts measured in lengths, knots and strides, with the dead surveyor's four-sign index printed at their heads; an **anomaly column** in which every sheet, in every hand, for six years carries the one word *Total* (an entry, not a sum; no figure); "More than four" (Karis, counting distinct sign-groups; she gives no number); the Fallow completion report is the last, loose sheet, and carries **five strokes for a name and a count of six** (locked Book 7 ch40, ch43), not five names. (2) **The page:** a COPY in Vastin's own hand of one line from an old register, carried in oilcloth in his coat: "—of the Architect: see the lower archive at Treswick, which holds it in full—". "The Architect" is a title, not a name, and a word Karis has never met in any stratum. It is never called a leaf; **the leaf has not appeared**. (3) **The technician's sheet:** the two protected lines with a date between them, a brush bar across what followed, and Karis's *not read*. **The date is a Compact date, a registry year and a day in it, and is never printed as figures** (the source gives none; no owner decision is needed). The office had filed the sheet at the end of the second row and it lies there again.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:266:**Vastin.** No office, no seal, no rank; he left the seal in a tray "some months" ago and walked three hundred miles. **No age is stated.** A bad knee; raw hands; a left hand that will not lie flat. **No Iron Wall has been shown or named.** He has handed over three things in his own order and holds Karis's receipt in his coat. He has said: that he holds no office and has no sanction; that the layer cannot be opened ("There is no key"), on the authority of the office's own page; that the one line which should name its maker cites a title and sends its reader to Treswick's lower archive (his own copy of it); that nothing of his follows him and the Stair's rim is not his; that the pending paper is unchanged; why he did not take it to a council. He knows the six by name. **He does not know** the mechanism, what Cael carries, the instruments' behaviour in Cael's hand, Karis's case or the sites (beyond hearing Brom say "four on the hide" and Lira name the Stair), who held the abstracts, which classification event the sheet means, or what is under the bar. He has not weighed the sheet's date. He has not read the flat's last row through, and nothing has been said of a directive or an objection. He has not asked to join and nobody has spoken of it. He was sent to bed, began to argue twice, took four stairs fast and the rest slowly; whether that was the order or the knee is not settled.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:278:**Words said aloud for the first time.** *Vastin* (Seln, at the landing). *Treswick* by Vastin, at noon, from the other side. On paper only, and said by nobody: the title on the page. Not said aloud by anybody in chapters 10–12: *west*.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:305:- **Vastin's three reflexes** (a directive; a classification; "This has to go up") and **the first thing Seln ever taught anyone:** "You keep drafting orders." / "Habit." / "Out here the habit's the tell." / "Draft nothing. Just look." **Cleon** was named for the first time (Vastin: "Treswick,"; Karis: "The archive under it. Cleon."; Cael: "Who's Cleon?"); OWNER-pending #52 verbatim, as Karis's own rounding.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:308:- **The rise (the 281st, near noon):** Treswick a day's walk off — a bluff in a river loop, three walls in tiers, a pale steady light on the crown that Cael does not look at. **Cael laid his hand on the page** (the author's; kept); it stays in its oilcloth in Karis's coat.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:339:- **Treswick from the rise.** A green plain with hedged fields; a river out of the north in loops; a bluff in the nearest loop; three walls in steps; a small pale steady light above the highest roofs. A day's walk off.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:345:**Calendar.** A little before noon on the **two hundred and eighty-first day past the Line**, going down the western side of the long rise, a day's walk from Treswick. Days on the page: 278, 279, 280, 281. No season, month or weekday name; no figures for the technician's date; no count of years since the Kindling.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:349:**Cael.** Nineteen. **Ten fragments; no eleventh.** **Deployment thirty-two.** Left palm stung by Ember. He ruled on a job and has made no vow. **He has read the technician's date, laid it against the first line of his own file, and knows it for the day of his own Kindling. He has not written it, has told nobody, and has put no verb to it.** He said "You do now" to Vastin at the hold. He has written in the log, at Oryn's asking, that inside Treswick he does not go near the station. **He has laid his hand on the page once, on the rise, and Karis has it again.** He has seen the light on the crown and turned from it. He carries a box. He asked "Who's Cleon?" and has the name.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:386:- **Treswick/day:** it is a little before noon on day 281, at the top of the long rise, a day's walk from Treswick. The six have seen a bluff, river loops, three tiered walls and the pale steady station light; Cael turned his eyes to the lowest wall, and Lira has not yet performed the packet's unasked matching discipline (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:233–269`; `packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:24,43`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:388:**Movement 3 CLOSED (2026-10-11).** Same-author repair r1 (ch13, ch16–19; ch14–15 untouched): the eleven coordinator-applied fixes kept and their joins smoothed (Seln on the north bank beside the factor; Cael had not known that he would say "You do now,"; Vastin names the town); no number of places and no fifth place (Karis counted groups, not places; four matched to the hide; the other sheets' corners turned down, uncounted and undescribed); the second calendar cut (Seln knew the day because he had copied that line of Cael's file twice; Cael laid the date he knows against the sheet's, a figure at a time, twice); three tracked passages re-ordered; the ruler line verbatim at the stopped lamps sentence; the remark's hand unidentified; Brom counts the spring's three findings on his fingers; the loads and the closing file made to meet Movement 4 (**Vastin took the kit case against the letter of Oryn's "you're not to" and told Cael so at once; Oryn does not know**; he walks a shoulder off Cael's left from a dozen strides down the rise). Sol recheck: CLOSE WITH LINE FIXES; all tracked passages RESOLVED; every binding ruling borne out; the settled rulings (the cut's staging, thirty-two, Oryn's past, the hand on the page) confirmed in the surviving prose. Two fixes applied by the coordinator: ch16 "Two days ago, at a board" (was three); ch18 Seln "has spent fifteen years among the seat's paper" (he copied for twelve). The "New canon minted" and "State at movement end" sections above were refreshed from the post-repair author report. Final: 34,751 prose words (about 2% over; accepted — the added scene carries the loads and the seam); gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected (16 protected). Purse 138 marks; deployment thirty-two; day 281, near noon, going down off the rise toward Treswick.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:395:- **The road hold lifts at the first hedge** below the rise: on a town's ground a person may speak and **nobody declares** (there a declaration draws a clerk, not a hound). **The Line at Treswick is the river; the sill lies under the outer gate.** Wayposts at nine, six and three miles; the six slept at the three-mile pull-in on the 281st.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:398:- **Treswick (the 282nd).** The grey bridge on five piers is of dark, dry-laid stone with no mortar and is OLDER than the walls (Karis, from the masons' fitting of the pale stone to it); the same dark stone is the registry's three lowest courses, the undercroft's end and the frame of the iron door. The outer gate: one keeper counts feet on a bead-frame ("Six"); another writes only loads that come on wheels to be sold. **No name of the six was written.** The outer district works by brokers' slate boards and counted labour: cards with a coloured edge (blue to the second wall, buff to the third) carry a figure, are counted in with a pen and torn at each gate, and are good for the day named. **Iron passes the second wall by right, Bronze the third** — on a certificate that is read out and WRITTEN. The smith's two forges (charcoal; an Ember's held bed for a horse with a blue band): Brom, "They shoe by the tier." (protected). The rope-walk: sixty yards of four-strand priced (no figure printed) and to be bought going out; the Lowmarch debt stands. **The inn with two doors** (the painted door has a book; the yard half-door takes money): the long loft over the stable for a week from the 282nd, the pot at dusk, seven bowls; two marks paid; **purse 136**. Lira hung a blanket over the loft's uphill window.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:399:- **Vastin:** "I have papers I will not show. I want that said once, so that nobody asks twice." (three sheets under one seal, in oilskin, beside Karis's receipt). He has certified Treswick on four occasions. His cutaway: "the first honest district". He has sat three times; no age; no wall; **the right knee is day five of thirty on the 284th**; he came down twenty-two steps and caught one slip with his left hand.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:415:- **Where the Line is at Treswick.** The river is the Line; the sill (one long stone, worn hollow, a socket at each end for a bar) lies under the outer gate's arch. The hedged fields east of the bridge are "ground that the town uses and does not own", worked to the foot of the moor, with a watch that rides as far as the fields go. **The road's hold is lifted at the first hedge, in one half only:** they may speak; nobody declares ("Out there a declaration draws a thing with teeth. In here it draws a clerk.").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:437:**Calendar.** The forenoon of the **two hundred and eighty-fourth day past the Line**, under Treswick, on the head of the stair inside the iron door. Days on the page: 281 (the rise's foot; the posts; the three-mile pull-in), 282 (the bridge; the outer gate; the district; the inn; the district's edge; Seln's report), 283 (the cook-house at noon; the route; the evening), 284 (the inn yard at dawn; the second bell; two gates; the lane; the cut; the yard; the clerk; the door). Oryn: the first gate at dusk on the 282nd and the morning of the 283rd; the second gate from the night of the 283rd to first light on the 284th. No season, month or weekday name; no figure for the technician's date; no count of years since the Kindling.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:478:**Movement 4 CLOSED (2026-10-11).** Same-author repair r1 (a bounded line repair; nothing re-staged): the nine coordinator-applied fixes kept and their joins smoothed (the boulder image made to agree with "*no length*"; Karis looks at three boxes and a case before "Four hands."; the cook-house questions after the restored exchange are of method only; "Four." given to Cael at the parapet); Vastin's refusal recomposed to locked Book 6 (the Ostrand case stated as the cause, twice, and not taken back; beside it "I had kept my hand off a door for a sound reason, and I was thankful of it for a poor one"; entered "on a form which has no line for why"); the two tracked passages in ch26 re-ordered (Lira prices the ladder aloud and shoulders the box before Cael understands; the clerk writes *four* and blots it before he looks at a face, then opens the door, looks at Vastin, opens his mouth and shuts it); Wind's ceiling removed; **Cleon's name comes to Cael at the cook-house counter and is then read on the card — nobody has said it aloud**; second tellings of the name-versus-count idea trimmed. Sol recheck: CLOSE WITH LINE FIXES; both tracked passages RESOLVED; every binding ruling borne out; the day arithmetic confirmed (161 days since the last self-reading; four days since the board; 282 days since the first sill; Oryn's gates). One punctuation fix applied by the coordinator (a broken dialogue join in ch21). The "New canon minted" and "State at movement end" sections above were refreshed from the post-repair author report. Final: 35,179 prose words; gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected (12 protected). Purse 136 marks; deployment thirty-two; ten fragments; the forenoon of day 284, inside the iron door under Treswick.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:485:- **The Deepstacks.** Inside the iron door: a sliding bar; **twenty-seven steps of the dark stone in three flights of nine**; a cross-passage; three galleries side by side, cut in the bluff's pale bedded rock (the rock was cut first; the dark stone laid against it second; the town's mortared work third — Karis's first finding, undated). **The middle gallery** is about a hundred and ten strides, shelved to the roof with nothing ticketed; sorting tables from ninety strides; Cleon's sloped desk at the end under a fixed lamp on an iron arm, with a shelf above it (a cup, a jar, a thick bundle tied both ways in brown tape, and a black oak plank in sacking). The eastern gallery holds the old town's tall tally-books; the western, quarrymen's gear. **The fifty-two sheets lie on three cleared tables, 11 / 29 / 12 (the Ring, the Stair, the Hall), as they lay on the floors, and stay there; the boxes go up at the clerk's bell each evening and come down each morning on a fresh card.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:488:- **The yard door, the 285th.** The clerk's form had no line for matter that had gone up and come back; he asked one question ("The same?") and was about to send up for the under-registrar. **Vastin gave his old name, rank and office aloud** (protected: "Vastin. Archmarshal, Compact enforcement. You'll find the name is —"); the clerk's pen came up and **wrote nothing of it**. **Seln, posing as a porter on the hatch's bench, answered truthfully** (protected, whole: "He's on the count. Four hands, same as yesterday, entered by the practitioner and answered for by her, and the form asks what a hand's for, not what he was. The researcher's at your counter and she'll want to be told we're through,"). The clerk wrote *The same* and *four*, and has done so each day since. **The cost: a Treswick registry clerk now knows Seln's face and voice.** "I'm sorry." (Vastin) / "Don't be sorry. Be nobody." (Seln). Seln watches from the roof above the cut's head from then on. No restricted name has been written.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:504:- **The Deepstacks' ground.** Inside the iron door a bar of black iron as long as a man's arm, shot from within. A stair of the dark dry-laid stone, **twenty-seven steps in three flights of nine**, with two landings, low-roofed, unworn. At its foot a cross-way a dozen strides long, lined with the dark stone; off it **three galleries side by side**, each as broad as a cart, cut in the bluff's pale bedded rock with a pick. **The middle gallery** is shelved to the roof in bays divided by uprights of black oak, about a hundred and ten strides long; nothing on its shelves has a ticket (some bundles have tags on their under sides). From ninety strides the old town's sorting tables stand end to end down the middle; at the end, against the cut rock, a high sloped desk of black oak with a lamp in a glass chimney on an iron arm, and a shelf above it (a cup, a jar of water, a thick bundle tied both ways in brown tape, and the board in sacking). **The eastern gallery** holds the old town's ledgers; its tall books stand as high as the roof and are reached by ladders. **The western gallery** is the quarry's own: the board lay on its bottom shelf under quarrymen's wedges. The cold does not move; a flame stands straight; no sound comes down from the registry. **On the 284th** he gave his orders for the three tables over his shoulder, with his finger still on its line, and told them to get their loads off; when Cael next looked he was standing at the first bare table and the leaf lay face upward on the desk with nothing across it to keep the place. The Hall's table is not six strides from the desk, and nothing said there is too low to be heard at it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:519:- **Seln's night (the 286th).** The district is empty at night; a watch's handcart goes its round with a lantern; the blue gate is shut, with a brazier in the arch. He sat on the leads of **the chandler's warehouse on the ring road, the tallest roof below the blue gate** (four floors, a hoist-beam, an outside stair with no door). The case weighs "something under three pounds"; its key is in his waistcoat. **Every registry on the Line has three doors**: the front for names; the yard for loads; and a returns hatch at the side, with a lamp and a night clerk, where a courier lays a sealed thing at any hour and neither may ask the other a question: "A registry enters what is laid on its ledge." Treswick's is down a passage off the square's eastern corner. He considered the hatch and put it by; he considered leaving the case on the Deepstacks' unticketed shelves and saw that for filing; he ruled nothing. He marked that a clerk had seen his face and that nothing had fallen.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:530:**Calendar.** The night of the **two hundred and ninetieth day past the Line**, in the long loft at Treswick. Days on the page: 284 (the Deepstacks), 285 (the hatch; the lamp), 286 (the dray; the board; Seln's roof at night), 287 (the morning log; the figures; four times; Cleon's week and close; the parapet), 288 (the test; ten letters; "We are looked at"), 289 (the loft paid; the ladders; thirteen), 290 (fourteen; the alley; the loft). No season, month or weekday name; no figure for the technician's date; no count of years since the Kindling.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:542:**Seln.** Shadow; Bronze. A clerk of the Treswick registry knows his face and has heard him speak. He watches from the roof over the cut. He has looked at the registry, its three doors and the station's light from a roof, with the case on him, and has ruled nothing. **The case is on him, shut; its contents are not named in this movement.** He has the better half of his cord and the stave. He has seen the same boots three times.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:561:- **Deepstacks geography and custody.** Inside the iron door: black sliding bar; twenty-seven dark-stone steps in three flights; a short cross-way; three side-by-side galleries. Middle gallery: roughly 110 strides, shelving to the roof, old sorting tables from ninety strides, Cleon's sloped desk and fixed lamp at the end, with cup/jar/brown-taped bundle/board shelf above. Eastern gallery: tall old-town ledgers and ladders. Western gallery: quarry material, where the board was found. Fifty-two first copies remain on three tables; the board is against the third and the bundle remains tied on the shelf (`chapter-27.md:5–121`; `chapter-30.md:263–273`; `chapter-33.md:305`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:571:- **Seln and the case.** Seln is at the ladder head/roof watch, knows the same altered boots through three sightings, and has the better half of his cord and the stave. A Treswick clerk knows his face and voice. His case is on him and **shut**; five people know its contents from Book 6, but this movement names none. He looked at the registry/front-yard-returns-door choice and decided nothing (`chapter-30.md:3–151`; `chapter-33.md:183,247–275`; `book-06 chapter-38.md:167`; `book-06 chapter-39.md:5,15,217`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:113`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:573:**Movement 5 CLOSED (2026-10-12).** Same-author repair r1 (ch27–31; ch32–33 untouched apart from the eleventh's lines set in italics): the eight coordinator-applied fixes kept and re-joined — **ch27's scene at the Hall's table now turns on Cleon** (Cael's "Then what is it?" goes to Karis, who does not answer; Cleon, eyes shut at his desk, says the "Being believed" unit to himself in the hearing of five; Karis tells Brom who has believed him; Cleon opens his eyes for "Give me a week."; **Karis then asks the five in her own words — "I should like his week" — and Cael says it is hers**); ch30, Cleon re-sets his own week from the 287th (half the first went on his own page each morning; that is put by); ch31's opening keeps only her side of being believed; Seln's line at the hatch whole, with the narration noting that he said nothing that was not in the clerk's own book or at his ledge, "and he had said *we*, which lay in no book at all"; Cleon's close whole with the author's joins. The tracked passage re-ordered (Cleon gives his table orders over his shoulder with his finger on his line; when Cael looks again the chair is empty and the leaf lies face up, unmarked); two physical anchors in the cipher proof; restated method compressed; first-use anchors added. Sol recheck: **CLOSE, no line fixes**; the tracked passage RESOLVED; every binding ruling borne out; the coordinator's ruling on the eleventh's lines (Cael's own cataloguing, in italics, not a system block) treated as settled and consistent on the page. The "New canon minted" and "State at movement end" sections above were refreshed from the post-repair author report. Final: 35,987 prose words; gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected (17 protected). Purse 134 marks; deployment thirty-two; **eleven fragments**; the night of day 290, in the loft at Treswick.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:636:**Calendar.** The night of the **two hundred and ninety-third day past the Line**, in the long loft at Treswick. Days on the page: 291 (the ladder; the carts' street; the beam; the hatch; the gallery; the inside; the twelfth; the telling; the stair), the night of 291–292 (the tail), 292 (below; the parcel; the meal; the inventory; the light), Oryn at her fourth gate from dusk on the 292nd to first light on the 293rd, 293 (the leaf; the chronicle; the copy; Vastin's afternoon and stair; the street; the yard fire). No season, month or weekday name; no figure for the technician's date; no count of years since the Kindling.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:688:- **The road east (the 295th–297th).** The rope: **sixty yards of four-strand, two marks (purse 128)**, bought at the walk under Treswick's wall and paid to the Lowmarch ferryman, who waived the fare; the debt is closed. Out by the outer arch: six out as six in, none written. **The bridge: five piers counted; the crown not looked at** ("the promise held to the gate and is done; the not looking was mine"). The spring, with the wind in their faces. The fork-stone passed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:692:- **Lowmarch (the 297th).** Pike's twelfth line is the clearance (*Eight. Twenty; paid.*); the thirteenth, protected: *Treswick. Survey read. Bearing.*, with price and outcome left empty and said to be empty. **Cael read it the right way up, from Pike's side of the bench.** Pike put a DAY against the season line (nothing printed; "Eleventh. And dated."). **Teague's term, taken as a contract** (protected: "Ten of us on a wall's count. Your six and my four." … "Contract. Not more than that. I'll not have it called more." / "The wall's still the wall." — all Teague's): **ten on the count — Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln, Vastin; Teague, the tall man with the spear, the bow, the young one; NEITHER healer**; shares and costs by the count; **the field is Teague's** (Cael: "It's yours. I'd have asked you to take it."); the reading is Karis's ("You'll be asked."). The wall has a month on it and is not stood before the month is out. No hand was offered; the cloth still reads first and eleventh.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:754:**Where everyone is.** Twelve and a mule, in file: Seln ahead; the tall man; Teague, with Cael at his left shoulder a stride back; Lira; the young one; Karis, the two healers and the brown mule in the middle; Brom; Vastin a stride behind him; the bow last. Cleon is under Treswick with the leaf, the chronicle and the board. Pike is at Lowmarch.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:770:**Teague and his crew.** The contract is taken: ten on the count; shares and costs by the count; the field his; the reading Karis's. *"The wall's still the wall." and the Force line are his.* His wrist was used once, on a cart, and is wrapped in linen under the leather. He has not said "Noted." The tall man, the bow and the older healer have said nothing to the six. What his four have been told: that an office's survey was read at Treswick and gave a bearing; that the wall has a month on it; the four figures on the hide and "three days past the iron". Not told: the leaf, the list, the mechanism, any fragment, the date, who Vastin was.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:867:**Where everyone is.** Twelve and a mule in one camp under the step, at one fire in two halves: Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln, Vastin; Teague, the tall man, the broad man, the young one, the older healer; Oryn and the brown mule. Seln is back from the gap and is to look again at first light; nobody moves until he has. Cleon is under Treswick. Pike is at Lowmarch. The watch's seven went east along the perimeter path on the morning of the 304th and have not been seen since.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:940:- **The team (54:23–35; 55:279–295; 56:71–83).** Nine (Seln would not swear to ten), hooded, cloths tied; three crossbows; one maul-man; the Span's seven among them by a cough. They call nothing and loose without a word. They leave on two low whistled notes, the same two as in the stepped cut under Treswick. No face, no paper, no mark on anything they left.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:985:- Cleon is under Treswick; Pike at Lowmarch; Hesk at Denvash (not on the page).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:1072:- Teague's grief and after-next-thaw return; Oryn's three holds and after-thaw map term; Cleon under Treswick; faceless faction; Seln's undecided case; Cael's two acquisition debts all remain live (`chapter-56.md:3–59`; `chapter-57.md:3–99`; `chapter-60.md:103–265`; `BOOK_MAP.md:40–45,490`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/pre-B7-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:28:- **The long table** (midday). The Seln–Vastin doorway exchange, verbatim; these are their first words to each other. Vastin says the short thing: he resigned or walked out. Brom: "Three hundred miles is a demonstration." The layer: Karis supplies its existence ("Under every station on the continent. I said so at a table in the autumn"). Vastin's new fact: "Not *will not*. *Cannot.* There is no key." The name is a citation to a designer, and the trail ends at Treswick. Vastin then has nothing to do. Lira asks "Why us." Oryn notices the knee: "Then I still haven't asked." "What follows you": nothing that crosses the Line, and the Stair's rim "is not mine". Cael remembers the Book 6 sentence and says only, "Ask him the thing you want to ask him." Karis asks. **Close (verbatim).**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-004/recheck-r1.md:57:- The road, bridge, Treswick wall sequence, river/Line placement, gate colours, cards, tier rights, and porter route all agree with the ruling.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-004/recheck-r1.md:77:The exit state matches `packets/MOVEMENT-005.md`: all five travellers and their loads are inside the lockless iron door beneath Treswick; Cleon stands at the stair head with his single lamp; the clerk and Seln remain outside; the date is the 284th. Movement 5 can therefore open in the middle gallery with Cleon's lamp and the already-burning light without a seam contradiction.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/pre-B7-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:26:- **Lowmarch (297th).** Pike: *Treswick. Survey read. Bearing.* The price and outcome columns are left blank, and the season line is dated. Cael reads the line the right way up. **Teague's term and contract, verbatim:** ten on a wall's count; shares by count; the field is Teague's; the reading is Karis's. "Contract. Not more than that." / "The wall's still the wall." Cael prices it honestly: Teague is the better field captain, and the rival clock still runs.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-004/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:80:- **Where the Line is at Treswick.** The river is the Line; the sill (one long stone, worn hollow, a socket at each end for a bar) lies under the outer gate's arch. The hedged fields east of the bridge are "ground that the town uses and does not own", worked to the foot of the moor, with a watch that rides as far as the fields go. **The road's hold is lifted at the first hedge, in one half only:** they may speak; nobody declares ("Out there a declaration draws a thing with teeth. In here it draws a clerk.").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-004/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:103:**Calendar.** The forenoon of the **two hundred and eighty-fourth day past the Line**, under Treswick, on the head of the stair inside the iron door. Days on the page: 281 (the rise's foot; the posts; the three-mile pull-in), 282 (the bridge; the outer gate; the district; the inn; the district's edge; Seln's report), 283 (the cook-house at noon; the route; the evening), 284 (the inn yard at dawn; the second bell; two gates; the lane; the cut; the yard; the clerk; the door). Oryn: the first gate at dusk on the 282nd and the morning of the 283rd; the second gate from the night of the 283rd to first light on the 284th. No season, month or weekday name; no figure for the technician's date; no count of years since the Kindling.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-004/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:139:7. **Where the Line lies** (the river; the sill under the outer gate) and **the lifting of the hold at the first hedge**. No earlier text of this edition places the Line at Treswick.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/pre-B7-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:17:It is the morning of the 278th day. A new slip is pinned on Pike's plank: *Clearance. The cut below the shoulder hold, on the border road, two days west.* It pays twenty. Nobody has said Treswick aloud since the page. Vastin sits at the door end and is not on the sheet.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/pre-B7-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:29:- **First light (281st).** "Not the steps. Not the square." The mule goes north with Oryn. Cael turns at a quarter-mile. From the top of the rise he sees Treswick, and a pale steady light on its crown that he does not look at.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-002/review-cold-prompt.md:1103:"To an archive. The lower one, at a town on the Line." He said the name as a man reads out a place from a waybill, with no notion of what it would do. "Treswick."

