+3. First six: `The carter was in the river`
+   Last six: `told to by somebody who knew.`
+   Listening notes: Clean. Cael's Anchor refusal and read-based directions are audible; Brom, Seln and the carter retain distinct action and speech. No rescue count is lost.
+4. First six: `"Walk!" It was the ferryman's boy,`
+   Last six: `"He will," said Brom, very low.`
+   Listening notes: Clean. `Walk`/`Stand` belong to the ferryman's boy relaying Cael; Seln owns the `all four wheels` report. `She's wound a cart` is WOWND, not the injury noun.
+5. First six: `Pike had no slip for it,`
+   Last six: `that we learned how he did."`
+   Listening notes: Clean. Pike clearly distinguishes spoken report from ledger entry. The italic log and surveyor's line flatten coherently; deployment advances 28 → 29. `third site confirmed on bearing` remains document text.
+
