+- Sentence before: `"It's twenty," said Pike. "At the hold's own gate, on the factor's thumb, when the factor's walked it. That's a hold that's lost carts. It doesn't say what to. They never do; they'd have to pay more."`
+- Sentence after: `Cael read the slip a second time, as he read anything, and it was the last five words that he read.`
+- Ruling: Sound. Pike's speech ends fully; Cael's rereading supplies the beat formerly carried by the cut silence tag, with no false continuation of Pike's voice.
+
+### Protected-slip join — chapter 13
+
+- Sentence before: `Beside the words Pike had drawn a little road going between two heaps, and on the road something with four legs.`
+- Protected unit: `*Clearance. The cut below the shoulder hold, on the border road, two days west.*`
+- Sentence after: `"It's twenty," said Pike.`
+- Ruling: Sound. The narration announces the slip before the italic line, and Pike's named price statement cleanly returns to spoken voice.
