+## Chapter 14 — Carters Declare
+
+Scenes: 5
+
+1. First six: `The copper was on its stone`
+   Last six: `them, and face the road again.`
+   Listening notes: Clean. Vastin's quoted `old man with three carts` is another man, while the later `old man at a ditch` is unmistakably Vastin from position. Seln's hand calls and Vastin's reflection remain distinct.
+2. First six: `The road came up under the`
+   Last six: `you're called." "Nobody will," said Brom.`
+   Listening notes: Clean. The factor is stable as the unnamed speaker; Karis, Brom, Seln and Cael are tagged. The three lost carts, carter, two mules and five visible hounds are kept separate.
+3. First six: `From the hold's back wall a`
+   Last six: `wheels and not a stride further.`
+   Listening notes: Clean. Lira and Seln's count rises from three/four to five, explicitly as visible hounds; the concealed strip remains unknown. Terrain and cart positions are audibly coherent.
+4. First six: `Karis had her leaf of findings`
+   Last six: `out." "It's heard twice," said Cael.`
+   Listening notes: Clean. Karis's five doctrine lines, Cael's plan, Brom's rock choice and Oryn's linen position remain separately owned. Vastin's assigned position one stride behind Brom is explicit.
+5. First six: `They went into the cut from`
+   Last six: `all eight of them came on.`
+   Listening notes: Clean. Ember is the only declaration; Wind and the read are refused. Five visible hounds plus three hidden make eight, with no count drift. The cliffhanger ends on complete syntax.
+
+### Lane A second-ear join — chapter 14
+
+- Sentence before: `"I do not say it as a complaint. I am trying to enter it correctly. I have not gone into a room in forty years that did not turn to see who had come. I have just stood within fifty yards of a thing that hunts, and it went over me as it went over a bush. I find that I have no column for that."`
+- Edited join sentence: `He was a little out of breath, and he had kept his place, a dozen strides back, so that he had to pitch the words forward.`
+- Sentence after: `"You were a post. A post is what it doesn't look at."`
+- Ruling: Sound. Vastin owns the long speech and remains the only possible `He`; Cael's answer immediately afterward resets the second speaker.
