+## Supplemental audit after the full read
+
+- Coverage: fifteen complete chapter files, in order; seventy-eight scenes. A mechanical comparison found every recorded title, scene count, first six words and last six words exact, including punctuation and markdown emphasis.
+- Quotation marks: zero prose paragraphs with an odd number of straight quotation marks; zero curly quotation marks; zero instances of two closed quotations abutting with no beat (`." "`, `?" "`, `!" "`). There is no multi-paragraph speech in this range that relies on an intentionally open paragraph.
+- Italics and markdown: zero lines with an odd number of asterisks; no backticks, fences, bracketed all-caps forms or indented code. Forty-seven whole italic paragraphs/documents are balanced. The internal emphasis changes in mixed prose and dialogue are paired and intelligible after `fpaudio.py` strips the markers.
+- Scene breaks: every `---` has one blank line before and after.
+- Numerals: no Arabic numeral occurs in manuscript prose or displayed material in chapters 01–15. All days, money, distances, counts and tallies are written as words.
+- Accidental repetition: the repeated-word probe found only seven intentional `had had` constructions; no doubled-word typo.
+- Calendar and units: no named season, month, month order or English weekday; no metric unit. The modal `may`, the verb/noun `fall`, and four literal `inch` uses are not calendar hits and are clear aloud.
+- Continuity: deployment is twenty-seven → twenty-eight → twenty-nine → thirty. Purse is ninety-six → seventy-six → a hundred and sixteen → a hundred and eighteen. No echo disagrees.
+- Protected-pattern locations in range: chapter 05 ruler rule; chapter 06 west/Treswick speech; chapter 09 stance line and Seln/Vastin line; chapter 12 Oryn's `She's right` direction; chapter 13 clearance slip. Each is intact and its join is ruled above.
+- Long paragraphs after narrator flattening: ch06:257 (716), ch07:85 (716), ch10:25 (724), ch10:213 (763), ch12:123 (702), ch13:59 (771), ch15:101 (900).
